    "turn_text": "This podcast was recorded Thursday, June 27th at 1027 AM. Things may have changed by the time you hear this. Yeah, like now that it's legal, the smell of marijuana will be in the air at Comfest in Columbus this weekend, just like it has been since 1972. Let's talk politics. This is Snollygoster, WHO issue Public Media's weekly look at Ohio politics and all those Snollygosters, those shrewd politicians who look for your vote. I'm Mike Thompson. Coming up on the podcast, a new powerful lobby emerges at the Ohio Statehouse, and it wears short pants. But first, there have been six presidential elections this century. Four of the six have brought some claims of at least being unfair and at the most being stolen. In 2000, George W. Bush narrowly defeated Al Gore after the Florida recount was stopped by the US Supreme Court. In 2004, There were complaints by a few on the left that Bush unfairly won re-election because of alleged voter suppression efforts here in Ohio. Then came fairly routine elections in 2008 and 2012. Not too many complaints there. A very small number of Democrats claimed Hillary Clinton lost unfairly in 2016 because of alleged Russian interference on behalf of Donald Trump. Democratic Congressman Jim McGovern of Massachusetts on January 6, 2017 tried to stop the certification on the floor of the House. But for",
