    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "We all know what happened after that speech. The president's supporters stormed the Capitol and delayed the certification of Joe Biden's election. Now, let's be clear. There is a big difference here. In 2000, 2004, in 2016, the losing candidates, Al Gore, John Kerry, and Hillary Clinton, all conceded and embraced the peaceful transfer of power. The claims of stolen elections were largely pushed aside. The 2020 claims led to an insurrection, and the former president and his supporters continue to claim that election was stolen. It wasn't. Just like there is no evidence, the 2000, 2004, 2016 elections were stolen, there is no evidence 2020 was stolen. That brings us to the eve of the 2024 election. And the former president continues to warn of a rigged election months before the ballots are cast. And as a result, fair election advocates are mobilizing. One group is the Democracy Defense Project. It's a national organization. It is bipartisan. And it has a chapter right here in Ohio. It is led by Republican former Ohio Secretary of State Ken Blackwell and Democratic former Congressman Zach Space. And Zach Space joins us now. Congressman, welcome to Snollygoster.",
