    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "So it's a bipartisan effort to serve as essentially a counterweight to allegations that elections have been rigged or will be rigged. We've seen a lot of voices begin to speak up around this issue. since January 6th in particular. What makes this a little bit more unique than some of those voices is it's bipartisan and the organization has board members across eight states including Ohio. They've got Democrats and former Democratic and former Republican party officials as board members. And, you know, our purpose is to defend democracy. You've said it in your introduction. There have been questions raised about the democratic process now going back over 25 years, almost 25 years. And with the most serious ones being raised following the 2020 or actually leading up to and then following the 2020 election that resulted in the January 6 riots and to your point made earlier, continue to ring throughout the general populace and it's become an important message for a certain basis so the organizations intended to fight back against that to project to the voting public that the electoral process in this country is in fact working. that it does have integrity, and that if you're gonna use that issue as a means by which to either keep certain people at home by sowing doubt about the democratic process or energizing your base, or worse yet, calling into question the results of an election, that's very anti-democratic, it's very dangerous, and this organization is committed to fighting against it.",
