    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "ballots and votes? I know, I think our system associated with casting and counting votes works. So to answer your question, I think at the end of the day, those who are in political power, those who are in public office, have a responsibility to tell the truth and not to manipulate people based on lies. This organization is designed To put those who abdicate that responsibility on the spot. So, you know, this is going to take time. But we, you know, we need to ensure that those who are sworn into office and swear to abide by the Constitution that they mean it and. The hope and expectation would be that when you see an organization like the Democracy Defense Project out there in a bipartisan, and by the way, this is not just a bunch of Democrats and a few moderate Republicans. This organization is represented across the board of the political spectrum. We've got some very conservative, very liberal, and many moderate members on this board. And the hope is that many of these folks are respected in their communities, media, like yourself, listen to them when they talk, when these politicians choose to use these deceptive tactics that undermine our democratic process and its credibility integrity, then we're going to call them out. I wish that we didn't have to exist. I wish the people when they swore that oath would understand and incorporate the importance of this process and respect it and project that to their voters. But in many cases, they don't. Not at all. I mean, it just takes a few bad apples to ruin the whole bunch. But at this point, what we're hoping to do is continue to exert pressure with a drumbeat that's bipartisan nature that renders this kind of behavior unacceptable.",
