    "turn_text": "Time now for our Snollygoster of the Week segment where we honor the shrewdest politician or political move of the past seven days. This week it goes to a brand new and suddenly powerful lobby at the Statehouse. It's the Pickleball Lobby. The chairman of the House Finance Committee, Jay Edwards, had no idea so many Ohioans loved Pickleball until he saw the state's capital budget and all the Pickleball courts planned for communities around the state. By my count, lawmakers approved a dozen Pickleball court projects all around the state for a total of $1.9 million. You pickleballers, you're our Snullagusters of the week. Can a pickleball scandal be that far behind? One note, Richwood, Ohio, got a pickleball court in the capital budget. That's where our former colleague Steve Brown lives. The view from Richwood, remember? So maybe the view from Richwood will include a pickleball racket. Is that what they call them or they call them a paddle? I'm not a pickleballer. Anyway, stay tuned. That'll do it for this week's edition of Snollygoster, which is part of the NPR Network. As always, please, to be sure to leave us a good review on Apple Podcast, wherever you get your podcast, and just tell your friends about us. For our student producer, Katie Genius, our digital producer, Michael Dibonos, and our audio engineer, Dalton Jones, I'm Mike Thompson for Snollygoster from W.O.H.U. Public Media.",
